01:19.660 --> 01:22.470
I was made to hit in America

01:22.470 --> 01:25.240
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.240 --> 01:33.110
I was made to hit in America

01:41.590 --> 01:44.260
So, how was it?

01:44.260 --> 01:47.090
Pretty scary, that Leon Sykes.

01:47.090 --> 01:49.820
Will we be able to go on at Grateful Sound?

01:55.100 --> 01:57.440
He said he'd have to look into it.

01:57.440 --> 01:59.040
Look into it, huh?

01:59.040 --> 02:01.270
Just make sure you pay back the money

02:01.270 --> 02:04.110
for your expenses within this month, okay?

02:04.110 --> 02:08.710
He's the kind of guy who'd
kill Erica Blige for money.

02:09.780 --> 02:12.780
Yeah...I'll be careful.

02:12.780 --> 02:15.290
Don't want to lose my life over that.

02:15.290 --> 02:19.120
Anyways...Pay it back quickly, okay?

02:19.120 --> 02:23.290
Hmph. Don't worry. I'm not
getting bumped off just yet.

02:26.460 --> 02:28.360
Just pay it back, 'kay?

02:36.140 --> 02:38.080
Hiromi-chan, you bought all these?

02:38.080 --> 02:40.080
Yeah, they're from a used-book store,

02:40.080 --> 02:43.580
but now I can learn lots of songs,
and play my heart out.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.920
You're really into it.

02:45.920 --> 02:49.250
I'll look bad if I owned a guitar
and couldn't play a tune.

02:49.250 --> 02:50.420
Yeah.

02:50.420 --> 02:53.930
But these books are so hard to read...

02:53.930 --> 02:56.430
I wouldn't depend on these books entirely.

02:56.430 --> 02:57.930
There are lots of mistakes here.

02:57.930 --> 03:01.770
Huh? Then how am I supposed to learn?

03:01.770 --> 03:07.140
Well, it's best to listen to
the songs and then copy them.

03:07.140 --> 03:09.270
But I think it's up to the individual.

03:09.270 --> 03:12.440
For me, I'd get a book
on how to play chords,

03:12.440 --> 03:15.070
and practice that like heck.

03:16.080 --> 03:20.120
Would those books show the
finger placement of the chords?

03:20.120 --> 03:23.960
Yup, you press the strings and strum.

03:23.960 --> 03:27.790
I just practiced learning those chords.

03:27.790 --> 03:30.960
Then were you able to
learn the songs by ear?

03:30.960 --> 03:35.800
Ahh...Well, I did ask others too.

03:35.800 --> 03:39.070
That's incredible!
You are a genius, Koyuki-kun!

03:39.070 --> 03:42.240
Oh-oh yeah? I think I'm pretty ordinary.

03:42.240 --> 03:45.080
I'd still say you've got a good ear though.

03:45.080 --> 03:48.750
Anyway, practice makes perfect, I guess.

03:48.750 --> 03:50.250
I don't care how gifted you may be,

03:50.250 --> 03:52.750
you don't just wake up
one day knowing all this.

03:52.750 --> 03:55.250
You really think so?

03:55.250 --> 03:57.420
I...really don't have
much else I'm good at,

03:57.420 --> 04:00.090
and I love playing the guitar...

04:00.090 --> 04:03.250
And I've never once
gotten tired of playing.

04:07.600 --> 04:10.090
Well, maybe just once...

04:13.940 --> 04:16.600
Uh! Yeah!

04:20.510 --> 04:23.950
You open up the door
with negative aura

04:23.950 --> 04:24.780
You say future is murky indeed...

