07:39.640 --> 07:41.650
-So, what do you think of Beck, Manager?

07:39.640 --> 07:41.650
-I think there is no way my life

07:41.650 --> 07:43.550
-fizzle out

07:43.550 --> 07:46.720
Looks like they won't be quitting
the live house for a while.

07:46.720 --> 07:49.390
You open up the door
with negative aura

07:49.390 --> 07:50.390
(I'm fed up fed up fed up)

07:50.390 --> 07:52.290
You say future is murky indeed...

07:52.290 --> 07:54.920
I'm sick of hearing gripe.

07:57.400 --> 07:59.230
Hey, did you see that Shibuya one?

07:59.230 --> 08:01.170
Yeah, Yoshito's so cool!

08:01.170 --> 08:02.660
I'm totally into him!

08:05.740 --> 08:08.230
"Yoshito-Shibuya Panic"

08:10.910 --> 08:13.080
That must have been
an excellent promotion.

08:13.080 --> 08:16.410
Seems like the Grateful Sound
tickets are selling well too.

08:16.410 --> 08:18.250
Shibuya Panic, huh?

08:18.250 --> 08:22.950
Sounds like a take on a promotion that
the Stones did long ago in New York.

08:22.950 --> 08:24.420
The Stones, huh?

08:24.420 --> 08:27.430
They're in a whole 'nother league from us.

08:27.430 --> 08:31.190
Hey, to each his own.
We'll just do things our way.

08:33.430 --> 08:35.930
Huh? Ryusuke-kun!

08:35.930 --> 08:38.340
Hmm? Oh, Koyuki.

08:38.340 --> 08:38.540
"Shiina Bookstore"

08:38.340 --> 08:38.540
Hmm? Oh, Koyuki.

08:38.540 --> 08:41.740
"Shiina Bookstore"

08:38.540 --> 08:41.740
We were on our way to the Fishing Hole.

08:41.740 --> 08:44.040
"Shiina Bookstore"

08:41.740 --> 08:44.040
I have something I wanted to give to Maho.

08:44.040 --> 08:46.310
"Shiina Bookstore"

08:44.040 --> 08:46.310
She's there now.

08:46.310 --> 08:48.780
"Fishing Hole"

08:51.050 --> 08:53.140
Hey there, Koyuki!

08:55.220 --> 08:57.890
Um, this...It's from my parents.

08:57.890 --> 08:59.220
What is it?

08:59.220 --> 09:00.460
It's Kishu Ume.
(Pickled plums, Kishu-style)

09:00.460 --> 09:02.860
You were gobbling them up the last time.

09:05.060 --> 09:06.730
Thanks.

09:06.730 --> 09:10.570
Oh, let me introduce you,
she's my classmate, Melanie.

09:10.570 --> 09:13.070
F-fine, thank you. How are you?

09:13.070 --> 09:15.660
No one's asking how you're doing!

09:17.240 --> 09:18.580
You're funny.

09:18.580 --> 09:19.910
J-Japanese?

09:19.910 --> 09:22.910
Yeah, despite the way she looks,
Melanie was born in Japan.

09:22.910 --> 09:25.480
She's fluent in Japanese. Don't sweat it.

09:25.480 --> 09:28.090
Maho stayed overnight at your place, right?

09:28.090 --> 09:29.750
Wasn't her teeth-grinding something else?

09:29.750 --> 09:31.760
Ah, well...no...

09:31.760 --> 09:34.430
Her teeth-grinding is unbelievable!

09:34.430 --> 09:36.530
Even Yoshito said so.

09:36.530 --> 09:37.930
Oh, shut up!

09:37.930 --> 09:39.800
Why are you talking about that?

09:39.800 --> 09:41.200
I see...

09:41.200 --> 09:41.990
Huh?

09:49.210 --> 09:54.410
For Maho, it's nothing unusual
to sleep over at a friend's house...

09:55.610 --> 09:58.840
I guess I was the only one
getting all nervous over it.

10:05.720 --> 10:08.620
Americans are so progressive...

10:11.060 --> 10:12.730
Huh? Chiba's going to be there?

10:12.730 --> 10:15.730
Yup, he said he'll be on about 10 o'clock.

10:15.730 --> 10:20.740
He said if we mention his name at
the door, they'll let us in for free.

10:20.740 --> 10:23.300
That Chiba...What's he planning?

10:25.740 --> 10:26.910
Ah!

10:26.910 --> 10:29.410
Wake up at 11 in the morning,
the ideal break

10:29.410 --> 10:33.920
Turn off the switch from this rapid speed,
take a quick smoke, instantly hungry

10:33.920 --> 10:37.190
Eat move eat embrace relax embrace
sleep and relax again happiness

10:37.190 --> 10:41.690
Let the tension go mellow today
straight to the brain, simply flow

10:41.690 --> 10:45.030
Turning my ear, the rhythm of
the sound and words-die hard

10:45.030 --> 10:47.160
Right, how is it? This feeling!

10:50.870 --> 10:53.370
He was really in his element, huh.

10:53.370 --> 10:58.910
I wonder if Chiba plans to leave Beck,
and go with this band.

10:58.910 --> 11:01.280
No, this is his way of training.

11:01.280 --> 11:05.880
It really bothers him that he's the
only one who didn't see that dream.

11:05.880 --> 11:11.910
Chiba's the kind of guy who'd go tattoo
"Mongolian Chop Squad" on his back.

11:13.560 --> 11:17.390
What a fool...That Chiba.

11:17.390 --> 11:21.900
We wouldn't fire our band's front man
just because of some dream.

11:21.900 --> 11:23.060
Yeah.

11:39.580 --> 11:40.640
Huh?

11:43.920 --> 11:45.050
Maho?

11:49.430 --> 11:50.480
Yo!

11:52.730 --> 11:55.100
A-ho! A-ho!

11:58.770 --> 12:00.290
Ah, oh...

12:06.280 --> 12:08.780
That's strange, his wings are clipped,

12:08.780 --> 12:11.680
so he shouldn't be able
to fly away very far...

12:11.680 --> 12:14.290
When's Mr. Saito coming
back from his business trip?

12:14.290 --> 12:15.380
Tomorrow...

12:17.220 --> 12:20.460
Koyuki, you're really fond
of Mr. Saito, aren't you?

12:20.460 --> 12:24.660
You think so? Well, he is
my guitar instructor after all.

12:25.960 --> 12:29.330
Your mom was telling me
over breakfast last time...

12:29.330 --> 12:30.730
Huh? What did she say?

12:31.800 --> 12:34.840
That when you were little
you were a bit odd,

12:34.840 --> 12:37.070
and she was worried about your future.

12:37.070 --> 12:41.570
Hmm. Yeah, she says that once in a while.

12:44.180 --> 12:48.590
But I don't remember anything
from when I was little.

12:48.590 --> 12:50.920
So none of the things
she said I did seem real.

12:50.920 --> 12:53.260
Seems you were strange enough,

12:53.260 --> 12:55.420
climbing on top of the table
and singing and stuff...

12:56.760 --> 13:01.860
Yeah, but now, I'm just
an ordinary, teenage guy.

13:09.940 --> 13:11.780
Well, I better get going.

13:11.780 --> 13:12.440
Huh?

13:12.440 --> 13:15.780
Make sure you thank your mom
for me for the pickled plums.

13:15.780 --> 13:19.450
Oh, you're not coming over?

13:19.450 --> 13:22.450
I'll catch the last train out
tonight to get home.

13:22.450 --> 13:26.620
'Cause, when I'm alone with you,
I get kinda nervous

13:26.620 --> 13:28.960
and can't sleep too well.

13:28.960 --> 13:31.990
Uh...I'll walk you to the station.

13:33.430 --> 13:34.290
Uh-huh.

13:42.740 --> 13:47.580
Koyuki, I don't think
you're just an ordinary guy.

13:48.750 --> 13:50.250
You think so?

13:50.250 --> 13:53.420
I hope you find Page.

13:53.420 --> 13:54.080
Well, see yah!

13:54.080 --> 13:56.250
Thanks. Take care.

14:11.940 --> 14:15.370
In order to survive, without realizing it,

14:15.370 --> 14:18.600
I've adapted myself
to society's expectations.

14:21.950 --> 14:24.450
"If you live life by
other people's standards,

14:24.450 --> 14:28.910
then your life is no longer yours."
That's what Eddy said.

14:36.130 --> 14:40.060
If I really thought about what
it means to live life and to die,

14:40.060 --> 14:44.060
I may be the one who needs
to reassess things.

16:11.590 --> 16:16.590
What?! Page was singing along with you?
Then it must be a great song!

16:16.590 --> 16:19.930
Yeah, but I've only gotten
part of the refrain done.

16:19.930 --> 16:20.600
Hmm...

16:20.600 --> 16:24.270
If he didn't interrupt, I think I would
have had the whole song finished.

16:24.270 --> 16:28.030
But after struggling to
catch Page, it all went away.

16:29.610 --> 16:30.800
It just came to you?

16:32.280 --> 16:36.010
It seems so strange
when I think of it now.

16:37.210 --> 16:41.890
When I was trying to compose
a song, I couldn't at all.

16:41.890 --> 16:44.880
Then all of a sudden,
this melody just popped up in my head.

16:47.220 --> 16:50.890
Well, let's hear it!

16:50.890 --> 16:51.950
Okay.

17:36.540 --> 17:40.040
Koyuki, you really wrote that tune?

17:40.040 --> 17:40.980
Uh-huh.

17:46.050 --> 17:48.050
Then, where should I go?

17:48.050 --> 17:53.080
Okay, I know that. What time?
Okay. I'll be there.

18:18.420 --> 18:21.410
Hey, It's my first time
to ride on a helicopter.

18:25.420 --> 18:27.390
I brought this again, for Beck. Take it.

18:27.390 --> 18:28.790
"Dog Arnold's Bone" [Doggie Treats]

18:27.390 --> 18:28.790
I brought this again, for Beck. Take it.

18:28.790 --> 18:30.930
Hey, you fuckin' talk too much.

18:30.930 --> 18:32.430
Shoot me if you want, all right?

18:32.430 --> 18:35.430
You think I won't shoot you
right here, muthafucker?

18:35.430 --> 18:39.270
Hey, stop it! We're talking business here.

18:42.370 --> 18:44.880
So, where are you going?

18:44.880 --> 18:46.710
North.

18:46.710 --> 18:49.740
Damn, fucker! Always getting me
in trouble with the boss.

19:13.070 --> 19:16.230
Yukio! It's your favorite, stew!

19:28.090 --> 19:30.550
Damn, this fucker's
always doing this shit...

19:46.200 --> 19:49.710
Hello. Good morning.
Do you know who this is?

19:49.710 --> 19:51.880
There's only one woman that I know

19:51.880 --> 19:53.880
with a whiskey-soaked,
raspy voice like yours.

19:53.880 --> 19:55.050
It's been decided.

19:55.050 --> 19:58.850
You guys will be going on
the Grateful Sound stage.

19:58.850 --> 19:59.720
Yeah.

19:59.720 --> 20:04.720
There was a real push from Leon.
Even Ran couldn't resist.

20:04.720 --> 20:07.220
Hey Aunty, it's not finalized yet.

20:07.220 --> 20:09.230
Huh? What do you mean?

20:09.230 --> 20:11.730
I still have to run it
by the rest of the band.

20:11.730 --> 20:15.730
But don't you guys want to
perform at Grateful Sound?

20:15.730 --> 20:19.400
Yesterday, I met with Leon.
We even went to look at the stage.

20:19.400 --> 20:22.070
So...what happened?

20:22.070 --> 20:24.410
His terms were way too hard.

20:24.410 --> 20:27.000
I don't think we can go through with it.

20:32.580 --> 20:34.580
Hello, Ryusuke-kun?

20:34.580 --> 20:38.690
What's up? Koyuki, come help me
set up the fishing poles.

20:38.690 --> 20:41.280
Umm, I wanted you to listen to this.

21:10.720 --> 21:15.060
Hmm. I'm surprised
you wrote such a tune.

21:15.060 --> 21:16.060
Really?

21:16.060 --> 21:19.730
But the continuity is off.

21:19.730 --> 21:20.860
I see.

21:38.750 --> 21:42.090
All right! I've decided, Koyuki.

21:42.090 --> 21:43.420
Hmm? Decided what?

21:45.420 --> 21:49.430
We're going to appear at Grateful Sound!

21:49.430 --> 21:59.600
H-Hey! I-I-Is this for real?!
U-Us! Hah-hah!

21:59.600 --> 22:01.270
-Yeah!
-Dying Breed's not appearing?

22:01.270 --> 22:04.110
No, I don't want to trouble Eddy.

22:04.110 --> 22:08.510
I see. So what were Leon's terms?

22:11.110 --> 22:13.450
We'll talk about it later.

22:13.450 --> 22:16.280
Right now, I just want to focus
on improving the band's skills.

22:20.960 --> 22:23.130
